 Local development is provided separately by the Vite entry.
 
+## Persistent paper translations
+
+The customer translation extension requires both the frontend `dist/` and BFF
+`dist-server/` builds. Build with `npm run build`, then use the authenticated
+`npm start` runtime; the Vite development server alone does not provide the new
+persistent translation endpoints.
+
+Opening bilingual mode reads saved Chinese only. “开始翻译” explicitly starts a
+server task; “重新翻译” replaces a previous result only after all blocks succeed.
+Upload no longer pre-translates automatically. Failed/cancelled jobs keep the
+previous completed translation. Browser navigation does not cancel a server job;
+server restart cancels unfinished jobs but retains completed records.
+
+`DIKW_AGENT_SESSIONS_DIR/translations.sqlite` stores completed Chinese; persist the
+existing runtime directory volume. The customer deployment uses
+`/data/mbweb/translations.sqlite` inside `dikw-mbweb-data`. Cache keys include IAM
+issuer, stable Core ID, paper path, target language and format version; the source
+SHA-256 must still match. Readers authorized for this shared base reuse the same
+saved paper translation across browsers. Existing browser translation caches are
+not automatically imported. Original sources remain in Core.
+
+GET/POST `/web/papers/translation` and the job polling/cancel routes reuse the BFF
+session validation. POST also requires the configured public Origin. Only a job's
+initiator can cancel it. Database permissions are 0600 and writes are atomic;
+back up SQLite with its online backup API instead of copying a live WAL database.
+Do not publish databases or runtime credentials with source. No new provider key,
+IAM role, cookie or dependency version is introduced.
+
+Acceptance: first open must show “开始翻译” without a model request; generate once,
+reopen and restart the runtime to confirm stored Chinese; explicitly regenerate,
+then test failure/cancellation retains the previous complete result. Also verify
+anonymous endpoints are denied and a different reader can reuse a completed
+translation without generating another one.
+
 ## Configuration
 
 Required: DIKW_WEB_AUTH_MODE=oidc, DIKW_WEB_PUBLIC_URL, DIKW_WEB_CORE_ID,
