+# 2026-10-08 Persistent Chinese translations
+
+Customer extension on `v0.1.10` / `05a2568fee7db8be7776f5c511a19a6af2fcbf7f`,
+retaining the Maibo appearance patch and exact shared-package 0.1.4 cohort.
+
+- Opening bilingual mode only checks saved state; “开始翻译” explicitly submits.
+- The BFF reads the authoritative paper through the existing authenticated Core
+  proxy, validates the source hash, then saves only complete Chinese to SQLite.
+- Repeat visits, other authorized readers and runtime restarts reuse saved Chinese.
+- “重新翻译” generates a fresh result. Failure/cancellation leaves old Chinese intact.
+- Source changes require a new translation; browser navigation does not cancel
+  server work. In-flight jobs are not resumed after a runtime restart.
+- Upload indexing no longer starts an automatic translation.
+- Both frontend and BFF must be deployed. See [runtime details](../deployment.md#persistent-paper-translations).
+
+Validation: 37 test files / 215 tests passed, plus lint, types, production builds,
+format, bundle budget and boundary gate. The new tests cover explicit submission,
+reuse, source changes, partial/failure/cancel behavior, ownership, Origin and role
+checks, and a real shared BFF restart reusing SQLite with exactly one fake-model
+call. These tests use isolated synthetic source/auth/provider fixtures; they do
+not read customer papers, call a paid model or alter IAM. Full coverage/e2e was
+not executed. Browser layout checks also use clearly labelled synthetic data.
+
+Production deployment and remaining real-account acceptance are recorded separately
+in the PM handover repository under
+`deploy/parallel-test/releases/20261008-persistent-translation.md`; local test
+success alone is not a claim of customer data/provider acceptance.
